IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `Singapore card reward programmes — the shared domain`

-- ===========================================================================
-- THE SHARED ONTOLOGY for the twelve card reward programmes, written from
-- reading the held issuer documents TOGETHER (registers/source-bundle.json)
-- before any rule was written.
-- Private contract text, NOT law, and nothing here is advice about what any
-- card will actually pay.
--
-- SEAT. The seat is the CARDHOLDER'S: the person who holds the card and asks,
-- at the till or in the app, "what will this earn me?". Every fact below is one
-- that person can state at the moment of paying or from the month's
-- statement. The issuer's own determinations (whether a merchant is coded
-- online, whether a merchant counts as a Participating Merchant on the day)
-- are not hers to state and enter only as Unknown.
--
-- MEMBERSHIP TEST. A name belongs here iff a witness of ordinary competence
-- could depose to it WITHOUT reading any terms and conditions: "I tapped my
-- phone", "the statement shows MCC 5812", "I bought a plastic bag", "I have
-- spent S$412 at yuu merchants this month". Whether that earns 4 mpd or 0.4 is
-- a rule, and lives in the module for the document that says so.
--
-- NO RULES HERE. DECLARE only: no DECIDE, no MEANS, no #EVAL. Every issuer
-- module imports this one and adds no noun of its own.
--
-- THE FIVE DESIGN CHOICES THE DOCUMENTS FORCED
--
-- 1. Two axes for "contactless", and a value called Unknown. The cardholder
-- controls the CREDENTIAL and the PRESENTATION (physical card or wallet token;
-- tapped on a reader or used in an app); the merchant's acquirer controls the
-- INDICATOR the bank receives (online or card-present). Three issuers say in
-- terms that they do not determine it: DBS Woman's cl.13 ("These indicators
-- are decided by the merchant and their banker"), Citi 10X cl.6(ii) ("These
-- indicators are decided by the relevant merchant and/or their acquirer and
-- are not determined by Citibank"), HSBC Revolution cl.6 ("system indicators
-- which are determined by the merchants and the merchant's acquiring bank").
-- Three further issuers (UOB Preferred Visa, UOB Visa Signature, UOB PRVI) key
-- on how the card was presented or on the payment GATEWAY instead.
--
-- 2. Spend so far is a RECORD of pots, not a number on a card. The caps in the
-- documents belong to a pot (yuu's 28,800 bonus points; Preferred Visa's two
-- UNI$1,080 bonus pots; Visa Signature's two UNI$2,400 pots; Solitaire's
-- S$750 per category), several merchants and several MCCs draw on one pot, and
-- three kinds of figure travel with the month: the spend that earned the bonus
-- so far (for the cap), the spend that counts toward a floor (yuu's S$800
-- counts ALL Eligible Spend, not only yuu-merchant spend), and the number of
-- distinct merchants hit. `Month to date` therefore carries each of those in
-- the unit the document itself uses (points where the cap is in points,
-- Singapore dollars where it is in dollars).
--
-- 3. An answer carries a floor and a ceiling. Where a bonus waits on a
-- month-end condition the cardholder cannot yet know she will meet (yuu's S$800
-- and four merchants; PAssion's S$500 and five items; Standard Chartered's
-- S$800 and S$1,500 tiers), or on a fact only the merchant's acquirer knows,
-- the answer states what is certain NOW and what is earned if the condition
-- turns out well, and names the condition. It never picks the happy branch.
--
-- 4. Currency of reward is explicit and miles are MAYBE. A purchase earns yuu
-- Points, DBS Points, UNI$, HSBC Reward points, Citi ThankYou Points, Citi
-- Miles, 360° Rewards Points, Trust Miles or Max Miles. A document sometimes
-- fixes a conversion into miles (UNI$1 = 2 miles; 5,000 DBS Points = 10,000
-- miles; 1 yuu Point = 0.28 miles "or more") and sometimes does not (HSBC and
-- Citi ThankYou points); the answer's miles are `MAYBE NUMBER` and NOTHING is
-- not zero.
--
-- 5. Strings are not compared in rules. Catala has no strings and the
-- documents key exclusions by statement descriptor ("AMAZE*", "EZ-LINK*"), so
-- the statement line is classified ONCE, by the cardholder or by a caller, into
-- the closed enumerations below, and every rule reads only those. The
-- constructors name each counterparty or family a held document lists, not each
-- spelling.
--
-- TARGET. Written for the `main` compiler (build 98 or later) and checked with
-- the `unstable` one; see NOTES.md.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `The cards`

-- The products whose terms are held. Where an issuer's terms treat two
-- networks or two tiers differently, the network or tier is part of the card's
-- identity: DBS yuu Visa and American Express (yuu Appendix 1: "Points will
-- not be awarded for any transactions made with DBS yuu American Express
-- Card" at Charge+, and at 7-Eleven before 13 August 2026), Citi Rewards Visa
-- Signature and World Mastercard (10X cl.3: both are Eligible Cards, and the
-- Visa is being discontinued), the five UOB Lady's cards (Lady's Cards cl.2(a);
-- their caps differ), the three UOB PRVI Miles networks (PRVI cl.1(i);
-- SimplyGo accrues differently on the World Mastercard, cl.1(viii)), and the
-- two Citi PremierMiles networks.
DECLARE Card IS ONE OF
    `DBS yuu Visa`
    `DBS yuu American Express`
    `DBS Woman's World Mastercard`
    `DBS Woman's Card`
    `HSBC Revolution`
    `UOB Lady's Classic`
    `UOB Lady's Platinum`
    `UOB Lady's World Mastercard`
    `UOB Lady's Solitaire`
    `UOB Lady's Solitaire Metal`
    `POSB PAssion Debit`
    `Citi Rewards Visa Signature`
    `Citi Rewards World Mastercard`
    `UOB Preferred Visa`
    `UOB Visa Signature`
    `UOB PRVI Miles American Express`
    `UOB PRVI Miles World Mastercard`
    `UOB PRVI Miles Visa`
    `Standard Chartered Smart`
    `Trust Freedom`
    `Citi PremierMiles Visa`
    `Citi PremierMiles Mastercard`

-- What a purchase earns in. Each module states, from its own document, what
-- (if anything) the unit converts to.
DECLARE `Reward currency` IS ONE OF
    `yuu Points`
    `DBS Points`
    `UNI$`
    `HSBC Reward points`
    `Citi ThankYou Points`
    `Citi Miles`
    `360° Rewards Points`
    `Trust Miles`
    `Max Miles`


§§ `The purchase`

-- The currency the charge was made in, as the cardholder sees it. IDR, MYR,
-- THB and VND are named because PRVI Miles cl.1(x) pays a "Regional" rate in
-- exactly those four, and PAssion cl.10(a) treats MYR as a bonus item.
DECLARE Currency IS ONE OF
    `Singapore dollars`
    `Indonesian rupiah`
    `Malaysian ringgit`
    `Thai baht`
    `Vietnamese dong`
    `Another foreign currency`

-- Where the merchant's payment gateway sits. PRVI Miles cl.1(ix)-(x) and Visa
-- Signature cl.2(i) turn on it ("online transactions effected in foreign
-- currencies with merchants whose payment gateway sits in Singapore will not
-- be treated as overseas"). A cardholder often cannot tell, so Unknown is a
-- value.
DECLARE Gateway IS ONE OF
    `A gateway in Singapore`
    `A gateway in Indonesia`
    `A gateway in Malaysia`
    `A gateway in Thailand`
    `A gateway in Vietnam`
    `A gateway in another country`
    `Gateway not known`

-- Where the store is. yuu cl.8 ("transactions made in Singapore at") and
-- PAssion cl.9(d)/10(c) ("Participating Stores located outside of Singapore
-- ... not eligible") turn on it.
DECLARE `Store location` IS ONE OF
    `A store in Singapore`
    `A store outside Singapore`
    `Not a store`

-- How the cardholder paid. This is what she can see herself doing. It is NOT
-- the channel the bank sees (that is `Merchant indicator`).
--   * A wallet is Apple Pay, Google Pay or Samsung Pay (HSBC Revolution cl.5
--     names all three; UOB Preferred Visa cl.1(a)(vi) names the same three).
--   * "Tapped on a reader" is Visa payWave or Mastercard contactless at a
--     point-of-sale terminal. In-app and web wallet checkout is NOT tapped on a
--     reader: UOB Preferred Visa cl.1(a)(vi) ("In-app transactions made via
--     Apple Pay, Google Pay and Samsung Pay ... do not constitute 'Mobile
--     Contactless Transactions'") and Citi 10X cl.6(ii) ("excluding mobile
--     wallet") both draw that line.
--   * Magnetic Secure Transmission is a Samsung Pay mode that emulates a swipe;
--     UOB Visa Signature cl.2(iii) excludes it from Contactless.
DECLARE Presentation IS ONE OF
    `Physical card tapped on a reader`
    `Physical card inserted or swiped`
    `Wallet tapped on a reader`
    `Wallet by magnetic secure transmission`
    `Wallet used in an app or on a website`
    `Card number entered online`
    `Card details held on file by the merchant`
    `Card details given by telephone or mail order`
    `Recurring payment arrangement`

-- The system indicator the merchant's acquirer attaches when the transaction
-- is posted. Latent to the cardholder at the moment of paying, stable per
-- merchant. A cardholder who has seen this merchant post before can supply it;
-- one who has not supplies Unknown, and the rules answer under both branches.
DECLARE `Merchant indicator` IS ONE OF
    `Flags online`
    `Flags card-present`
    `Indicator not known`

-- Whether the charge has reached the card account. The documents count only
-- posted transactions (yuu cl.13; HSBC cl.4 "posted retail purchases"; PAssion
-- cl.13; Trust "must not be in an authorised, pending, or unposted status").
DECLARE `Posting status` IS ONE OF
    `Posted to the account`
    `Authorised but not posted`

-- What kind of charge it is, as a witness can say without reading any terms.
-- The union of the non-MCC exclusions the documents list.
--
-- TWO KINDS OF BILL, BECAUSE THE DOCUMENTS DIFFER. `Bill payment` is a payment
-- to a billing organisation THROUGH A BANK OR AGENT CHANNEL: internet or mobile
-- banking, AXS, a bank's bill-payment service. `Bill paid directly to the
-- biller on the card` is a common case: the card number entered
-- (or kept on file) in the biller's own site or app, as a Singtel, StarHub or
-- utility bill. Whether the second is a "bill payment" is exactly what several
-- documents leave to the reader: yuu Appendix 1 and PAssion Appendix 1 ("Singtel
-- ... Recurring bill payment and bill payments"), Citi 10X cl.5(iii) ("bill
-- payments (including via Citibank Online or via any other channel or agent)"),
-- UOB PRVI cl.1(ii)(b) ("all transactions in relation to or in connection with
-- bill payment"), Standard Chartered ("payments made to all billing
-- organisations using Standard Chartered Online Banking or mobile app").
-- Each issuer module says which kinds its clause reaches.
DECLARE `Charge kind` IS ONE OF
    `Retail purchase`
    `Bill payment`
    `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`
    `Top-up of a prepaid card or stored-value account`
    `Payment of funds to a payment service provider`
    `Instalment plan charge`
    `My Preferred Payment Plan charge`
    `Cash advance`
    `Balance transfer or funds transfer`
    `Fee, interest or finance charge`
    `Pre-authorisation`
    `Payment through UOB Payment Facility`
    `NETS or NETS-related transaction`
    `SmartPay or personal loan`
    `Transit-related transaction`

-- The counterparty or family a statement line names, for the exclusions that
-- the documents key by descriptor. One constructor per counterparty or family,
-- not per spelling: "AMAZE", "AMAZE*TRANSIT" and "AMAZE* AXS" are Amaze;
-- "EZ LINK", "EZ-LINK*", "EZLINK*" and "EzLink*" are EZ-Link. A statement line
-- no held document names is `Another description`.
DECLARE Descriptor IS ONE OF
    `AXS`
    `Amaze`
    `Amaze with a transit or payment counterparty`
    `EZ-Link`
    `FlashPay`
    `NETS VCashCard`
    `Transit Link`
    `TRANSIT`
    `SimplyGo as a descriptor`
    `SPL AUTO or SPL ATU or SPL ONLINE`
    `TL-ABT`
    `BUS/MRT as a descriptor`
    `Youtrip`
    `Razerpay`
    `SAM`
    `SingPost-SAM`
    `Sedap`
    `Sgebiz`
    `Singapore E-Business`
    `Singtel Dash`
    `ShopeePay`
    `SmoovPay`
    `Cantine`
    `Bagus`
    `iPayMy`
    `CardUp`
    `MatchMove Pay`
    `Fave or FavePay`
    `PayPal AXS Pte Ltd`
    `PayPal Bizconsulta or Capitalroya or Oandaasiapa`
    `Moneybookers`
    `Skrill`
    `OANDA`
    `Saxo`
    `IG Markets`
    `Plus500`
    `City Index`
    `SkyFX`
    `Banc de Binary`
    `RWS-Levy`
    `NORWDS`
    `A cryptocurrency or forex counterparty in DBS Table 2`
    `PayPal`
    `Another description`

-- The merchants some held document NAMES. A merchant no document names is
-- `Another merchant`. A shop's everyday name (Shopee, Tesla, ...) is not a noun
-- the documents use; where a document names Netflix (the Standard Chartered
-- Smart bonus merchants) it is a constructor here.
DECLARE Merchant IS ONE OF
    `Cold Storage`               -- yuu cl.8: Cold Storage, CS Fresh, Jasons Deli are ONE Participating Merchant
    `CS Fresh`
    `Jasons Deli`
    `Giant`                      -- yuu cl.8: Giant, Giant Hypermart, Giant Express
    `Guardian`
    `7-Eleven`
    `foodpanda`                  -- yuu cl.8: food delivery, panda mart, panda shops
    `Gojek Singapore`
    `SimplyGo`                   -- bus and train rides via SimplyGo (account-based ticketing)
    `Charge+`
    `CHAGEE`
    `SingtelShop!`
    `Singtel Exclusive Retailer`
    `Burger King`                -- Standard Chartered Smart bonus merchants
    `Domino's Pizza`
    `KFC`
    `McDonald's`
    `Pizza Hut`
    `Starbucks`
    `Subway`
    `The Coffee Bean & Tea Leaf`
    `Toast Box`
    `Ya Kun Kaya Toast`
    `Amazon Prime Video`
    `Disney+`
    `HBO GO`
    `iQIYI`
    `Netflix`
    `Spotify`
    `Viu`
    `YouTube`
    `SPC service station`        -- UOB Preferred Visa cl.2(f)(iv), Visa Signature cl.1(iv)(c), PRVI cl.1(ii)(d)
    `Shell service station`
    `Expedia PRVI site`          -- PRVI cl.2(i)
    `Agoda PRVI site`            -- PRVI cl.2(ii)
    `Another merchant`

-- The kind of outlet within a merchant, for the carve-outs the appendices
-- list by place: Cold Storage On The Go within Esso stations (yuu App. 1),
-- Changi Airport stores (yuu App. 1, Guardian and 7-Eleven), transit lounges
-- and vending machines (PAssion App. 1).
DECLARE Outlet IS ONE OF
    `An ordinary outlet`
    `Cold Storage On The Go within an Esso station`
    `A Changi Airport store`
    `An airport transit lounge or Budget Terminal outlet`
    `A vending machine`

-- What was bought or paid for, within a merchant, for the carve-outs the
-- appendices list by item (yuu App. 1; PAssion App. 1; Singtel, foodpanda,
-- SimplyGo, CHAGEE rows).
DECLARE Item IS ONE OF
    `An ordinary item`
    `A plastic bag`
    `Tobacco or cigarettes`
    `A delivery charge`
    `A service such as a mobile or EZ-Link reload`
    `A cash-like item such as a SIM top-up voucher`
    `A statutory service or product`
    `A DFI voucher or magazine`
    `A gift card or voucher being bought`
    `Listed infant milk formula`
    `Sushi or sashimi`
    `A lottery product, bill payment, top-up service or Qoo10 payment`
    `A foodpanda dine-in order`
    `A pandago order`
    `An order on a corporate account`
    `A pandapay wallet top-up`
    `A pandapro subscription`
    `A discount, voucher, delivery fee, platform fee or rider tip`
    `A Singtel corporate plan or sign-up`
    `A Singtel prepaid card top-up`
    `A Singtel bill payment`
    `A SimplyGo top-up`
    `A SimplyGo bus or train fare`
    `An order placed outside the merchant's own app`
    `An Expedia prepaid hotel booking`
    `An Expedia flight booking on a participating airline`
    `An Expedia package booking`
    `An Agoda prepaid hotel booking`
    `An Agoda hotel booking in Japan`
    `A hotel booking paid at the hotel`
    `An insurance premium`                       -- Standard Chartered exclusions: "any insurance premiums charged to your Card"
    `A betting payment`                          -- Standard Chartered exclusions: lottery tickets, casino gaming chips, off-track betting, wagers at race tracks

-- The clock a cap or floor runs on, as the document states it: the calendar
-- month, the card's statement period, or a window from card approval. And the
-- date it counts a transaction by, where the document says: the date the
-- transaction is made (settled), the date it is posted, or neither stated.
DECLARE `Period basis` IS ONE OF
    `Calendar month`
    `Statement period`
    `A window from card approval`

DECLARE `Date basis` IS ONE OF
    `Transaction date`
    `Posting date`
    `Not stated in the document`

-- Everything a witness can say about ONE charge. `amount in SGD` is the
-- Singapore-dollar amount posted to the account (inclusive of conversion and
-- commission), which is what every document computes on: yuu cl.22, Lady's
-- cl.10, SC Smart cl.16, PAssion cl.9(d). `mcc` is the four-digit merchant
-- category code on the statement or the acquirer's code; NOTHING if she does
-- not know it, and the rules that need it then say so.
DECLARE Purchase HAS
    `amount in SGD`      IS A NUMBER
    `date charged`       IS A DATE
    `date posted`        IS A DATE
    `posting status`     IS A `Posting status`
    `charge kind`        IS A `Charge kind`
    currency             IS A Currency
    gateway              IS A Gateway
    `store location`     IS A `Store location`
    presentation         IS A Presentation
    `merchant indicator` IS A `Merchant indicator`
    merchant             IS A Merchant
    outlet               IS AN Outlet
    item                 IS AN Item
    mcc                  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    descriptor           IS A Descriptor
    `later reversed`     IS A BOOLEAN


§§ `The cardholder`

-- Savings balance bands, shared by the two issuers whose bonus turns on a
-- deposit balance: UOB Lady's Savings Account Rewards cl.2.3 (Monthly Average
-- Balance) and HSBC Revolution cl.7.1 (Deposits ADB of S$50,000).
DECLARE `Savings band` IS ONE OF
    `Under S$10,000`
    `S$10,000 to S$49,999`
    `S$50,000 to S$99,999`
    `S$100,000 or more`

-- The seven categories a Lady's cardholder may elect (Lady's Cards Schedule 1).
DECLARE `Solitaire category` IS ONE OF
    `Beauty & Wellness`
    `Dining`
    `Entertainment`
    `Family`
    `Fashion`
    `Transport`
    `Travel`

-- UOB Visa Signature cl.2: the revised structure applies "immediately from the
-- card approval date" to cards approved on or after 1 July 2025; cards approved
-- before it moved to separate caps from the September 2025 statement.
DECLARE `Visa Signature vintage` IS ONE OF
    `Approved before 1 July 2025`
    `Approved on or after 1 July 2025`

-- What Trust Freedom card reward the cardholder chose at sign-up (the Spend &
-- Get promotion is for customers who "selected Miles as your reward type").
DECLARE `Trust reward choice` IS ONE OF
    `Miles`
    `Cashback`
    `Stockback`

-- Standing facts about the person and her account, true across the month,
-- grouped by the programme they belong to so that an issuer module takes only
-- the group it reads. A cardholder who does not hold a card leaves its group at
-- the default shown in each group's comment.
DECLARE `yuu holder` HAS
    `yuu account linked to the card`       IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `PAssion holder` HAS
    `People's Association member`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `yuu account linked to the PAssion card` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Lady's holder` HAS
    `elected categories`                   IS A LIST OF `Solitaire category`
    `Lady's Savings band`                  IS A `Savings band`

DECLARE `Revolution holder` HAS
    `Deposits ADB of S$50,000 in the sole Everyday Global Account` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Visa Signature holder` HAS
    vintage                                IS A `Visa Signature vintage`

DECLARE `Trust holder` HAS
    `reward choice`                        IS A `Trust reward choice`
    `new Trust credit card customer`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `card approved on`                     IS A DATE
    `Quest spend tiers in S$`              IS A LIST OF NUMBER

-- All the groups together, for a caller that holds several cards.
DECLARE Cardholder HAS
    yuu                                    IS A `yuu holder`
    `PAssion`                              IS A `PAssion holder`
    `Lady's`                               IS A `Lady's holder`
    `Revolution`                           IS A `Revolution holder`
    `Visa Signature`                       IS A `Visa Signature holder`
    `Trust`                                IS A `Trust holder`


§§ `The month so far`

-- What the month (or the issuer's own period for that pot) holds before this
-- purchase, in the unit the document's cap or floor uses. The caller computes
-- each figure over the period and on the date basis the module for that issuer
-- states; the module does not re-derive the period. A pot not yet touched is 0
-- or EMPTY. One small record per programme, so an issuer module takes only
-- the pots it reads.

-- DBS yuu (cl.7, cl.9, cl.10): the floor counts ALL Eligible Spend charged and
-- posted, the merchants are the distinct Participating Merchants hit, and the
-- cap is on bonus yuu Points.
DECLARE `yuu month` HAS
    `Eligible Spend posted`                IS A NUMBER
    `merchants hit`                        IS A LIST OF Merchant
    `bonus yuu Points earned`              IS A NUMBER

-- DBS Woman's (cl.19(b), cl.23(b)): "the first S$1,000 of online spend per
-- calendar month".
DECLARE `Woman's month` HAS
    `online spend accumulated`             IS A NUMBER

-- HSBC Revolution (cl.7.2): Eligible Transactions posted in the calendar month
-- and bonus points earned.
DECLARE `Revolution month` HAS
    `Eligible Transactions posted`         IS A NUMBER
    `Bonus Points earned`                  IS A NUMBER

-- UOB Lady's (cl.6): Bonus UNI$ so far, one figure per elected category, in the
-- order the categories are elected.
DECLARE `Lady's month` HAS
    `Bonus UNI$ by elected category`       IS A LIST OF NUMBER

-- PAssion (cl.4, cl.10): Qualified Spend, the items transacted, and the POSB
-- Bonus Points earned.
DECLARE `PAssion month` HAS
    `Qualified Spend`                      IS A NUMBER
    `items transacted`                     IS A LIST OF Merchant
    `ringgit spend made`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `POSB Bonus Points earned`             IS A NUMBER

-- Citi Rewards (cl.13): Bonus Points per statement month.
DECLARE `Citi month` HAS
    `Bonus Points earned`                  IS A NUMBER

-- UOB Preferred Visa (cl.3(c)): two separate pots.
DECLARE `Preferred Visa month` HAS
    `mobile contactless bonus UNI$`        IS A NUMBER
    `selected online bonus UNI$`           IS A NUMBER

-- UOB Visa Signature (cl.2): two separate pots, each with its own floor.
DECLARE `Visa Signature month` HAS
    `contactless and petrol spend`         IS A NUMBER
    `contactless and petrol UNI$10 earned` IS A NUMBER
    `overseas spend`                       IS A NUMBER
    `overseas UNI$10 earned`               IS A NUMBER

-- Standard Chartered Smart (cl.7): total Eligible Retail Transactions in the
-- statement month, bonus merchants and others together.
DECLARE `Smart month` HAS
    `Eligible Retail Transactions`         IS A NUMBER

-- Trust Spend & Get: cumulative posted qualifying spend since card approval.
DECLARE `Trust month` HAS
    `cumulative posted qualifying spend`   IS A NUMBER

-- UOB PRVI Miles American Express (cl.1(xi), cl.4): membership-year spend and
-- the quarter's overseas in-person spend.
DECLARE `PRVI month` HAS
    `membership-year spend`                IS A NUMBER
    `quarter overseas in-person spend`     IS A NUMBER

-- All the pots together, for a caller that holds several cards.
DECLARE `Month to date` HAS
    yuu                                    IS A `yuu month`
    `Woman's`                              IS A `Woman's month`
    `Revolution`                           IS A `Revolution month`
    `Lady's`                               IS A `Lady's month`
    `PAssion`                              IS A `PAssion month`
    `Citi`                                 IS A `Citi month`
    `Preferred Visa`                       IS A `Preferred Visa month`
    `Visa Signature`                       IS A `Visa Signature month`
    `Smart`                                IS A `Smart month`
    `Trust`                                IS A `Trust month`
    `PRVI`                                 IS A `PRVI month`


§§ `The answer`

-- What a month-end condition or a latent fact the answer waits on. An answer
-- names every one it depends on, so a reader never mistakes a conditional
-- figure for a settled one.
DECLARE Condition IS ONE OF
    `The merchant's indicator is not known`
    `The merchant's payment gateway is not known`
    `The merchant category code is not known`
    `yuu: S$800 of Eligible Spend and four Participating Merchants by month end`
    `PAssion: S$500 of Qualified Spend and the Tier items by month end`
    `Smart: the month's Eligible Retail Transactions reach S$800 or S$1,500`
    `Trust: the cumulative Quest spend tiers are reached`
    `Visa Signature: the S$1,000 statement-period floor is reached`
    `Lady's: the Savings band holds for the whole calendar month`
    `HSBC: the Deposits ADB holds for the whole calendar month`
    `The cardholder's statement date is not known`
    `The issuer's own product terms, which are not held, may exclude this spend`
    `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`

-- The pot a purchase draws bonus from, so that a caller can keep the month
-- so far. `Ladys category pot` carries which elected category.
DECLARE Pot IS ONE OF
    `No pot`
    `yuu bonus`
    `Woman's online`
    `Revolution bonus`
    `Lady's category` HAS category IS A `Solitaire category`
    `PAssion POSB bonus`
    `Citi 10X bonus`
    `Preferred Visa mobile contactless`
    `Preferred Visa selected online`
    `Visa Signature contactless and petrol`
    `Visa Signature overseas`
    `Trust Spend and Get`

-- One purchase on one card. `units` are in the reward currency. A floor and a
-- ceiling: `units certain` is what the held text guarantees now on the facts
-- given; `units at best` is what it pays if every named condition turns out
-- well. They are equal when `depends on` is EMPTY. `bonus units before cap`
-- is what the bonus tier would pay if the pot had room, so a caller can see
-- how much a cap took. Miles are MAYBE: NOTHING means the held documents fix
-- no conversion, not zero miles. The same holds for the Singapore-dollar cash
-- value of the units, which only the cash-rebate programmes state (the
-- Standard Chartered Smart card's 3,200 points for S$10; the yuu Point's 0.5%).
DECLARE `Earn answer` HAS
    card                     IS A Card
    `reward currency`        IS A `Reward currency`
    `units certain`          IS A NUMBER
    `units at best`          IS A NUMBER
    `bonus units before cap` IS A NUMBER
